{
  "about": "Tool-choice and story-coverage evaluation (STP-1805, STP-1808, from STP-1476). Each case is a user request from one STP-1476 user story or use case (stories), with the kind of input it carries, the server and mode it needs, the methods a model should use and must avoid, and the steering facts that must be in front of the model for that choice. Every story has at least one case; cases that share a pair id differ in their input or audience and so in their route. The evaluation is deterministic, with no model call: a fact is a set of case-insensitive regular expressions that must all match one text - a contract tool's description or edge cases, a description of one of this repo's tools, or the knowledge server's instructions. Routing lives in the contract's descriptions, not in MCP-side rules or overlays (STP-1808 rulings). A case passes when all its facts hold. Facts owned by this repo (owner mcp) must always hold; facts owned by the contract (owner contract) that fail are gaps, to fix upstream in the contract (proposal: docs/proposals/STP-1805-contract-wording.md), and the floor in test/tool-choice-eval.test.ts only goes up.",
  "stories": {
    "1a": "Help: operator help",
    "1b": "Help: developer help",
    "1c": "Help: deployment troubleshooting",
    "2.1": "Operating: language authoring",
    "2.2": "Operating: situational queries",
    "2.3": "Operating: editing existing objects",
    "2.4": "Operating: tasking and planning",
    "2.5": "Operating: mixed requests",
    "2.6": "Operating: session and scenario management",
    "3": "LLM-assisted code development",
    "4": "Headless integration and data exchange",
    "5": "Plan comprehension and analysis",
    "6": "Orders to plan",
    "7": "Event-driven monitoring",
    "8": "Training and doctrinal questions"
  },
  "facts": {
